---
title: Tytonidae
---
# Tytonidae

Tytonidae is the family of barn owls, separated from [[strigidae]] by a
heart-shaped facial disc and a serrated comb on the middle claw. The skull is
narrow, the legs long and feathered, and the eyes comparatively small for a
creature that forages in near-total darkness. Hearing rather than sight places
most prey: the two ear openings sit at different heights, so a sound reaches one
a fraction before the other and the difference resolves into an elevation. Some
twenty species are recognised, of which the [[barn-owl]] is much the most
widespread.
